    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478-a1">

                <pb facs="0862" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg762"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 51.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Ruelas.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States,</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 13,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my notes of the 21st and 26th
                    of June last, I am now instructed by my government to say to your excellency
                    that the accordance of asylum to the enemies of the United States flying over
                    the border when under pursuit involves in its apprehension an urgent obligation
                    on the part of the Mexican Government to disarm the Indians referred to in my
                    notes of the above dates, and a responsibility on the part of the Mexican
                    Government for any future inroads upon United States territory they may
                    make.</p>
                <p>I improve this opportunity to renew to your excellency the assurances of my very
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
